Story location metadata: overall='a medieval tavern'; starting='the tavern’s center'; setting='The tavern hall is a rectangular stone room, 30\u202fft east‑west by 20\u202fft north‑south. The back wall (north side) holds the single entrance: a wooden door centered on that wall, 4\u202fft wide and 7\u202fft tall, with its latch on the western half of the doorway.\n\nA polished wooden table sits in the central area directly north of the hearth; it is 12\u202fft east‑west by 6\u202fft north‑south. Rough‑spun cloth drapes over the top of this table, covering a width of 14\u202fft. The floor beneath is creaking wood that spans the entire hall.\n\nThe hearth occupies the middle of the room: its stone base measures 10\u202fft east‑west by 6\u202fft north‑south and rises 3\u202fft high. It extends one foot beyond each side of the counters that flank it. Two wooden counters, west and east, are positioned so their front edges align with the hearth’s western and eastern walls respectively; each counter is 8\u202fft long and 2\u202fft wide.\n\nBeside the hearth to the west lies an oil barrel: a 3‑foot diameter, 4‑foot tall wooden barrel whose base sits two feet from the front edge of the west counter. A goblin leans against this counter.\n\nFour lanterns hang above each table (the central table and one on each side counter). Each lantern is suspended by a wrought‑iron chain six feet above floor level.\n\nHigh bar stools line the north wall: five standard 2‑foot wide seats spaced evenly, with a special dragon‑shaped stool of 3\u202fft width occupying the space between the third and fourth standard stools. The back door remains fully accessible from any corner of the hall.'; location_state={'location': {'name': 'Tavern Hall', 'description': 'A rectangular stone hall measuring 30\u202fft east‑west by 20\u202fft north‑south, featuring a wooden floor, hearth, counters, table, barrels, lanterns, and bar stools.'}, 'anchors': [{'name': 'entrance', 'type': 'door', 'wall': 'north', 'wor